{{Quote|Imperius Unitada ober Totallex|[[Atrisian Basic]] motto and name of a [[Imperius Unitada ober Totallex|propaganda piece]], literally translating to "Empire united over all"|<ref name="Propaganda" />}}
The '''Galactic Empire''', also known as the '''First Galactic Empire''', the '''Imperial regime''', '''Palpatine's regime''', or simply the '''Empire''', and later as the '''Old Empire''', was a [[fascism|fascist]] and imperialist [[dictatorship]] that [[Proclamation of the New Order|replaced]] the [[Galactic Republic]] at the [[Battle of Utapau|end]] of the [[Clone Wars]]. Though the Empire rose to power by promising to bring order to [[the galaxy]], it oversaw a [[Time|period]] of [[Imperial Military|military]] rule and aggressive expansion. The subsequent [[Imperial Era]] would last only two [[Standard decade|decades]], for it was eventually overthrown by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] in the [[Galactic Civil War]], but not before the sovereign [[star system]]s of the [[galaxy]]'s [[Lesser Space|known regions]] had been largely conquered by the Empire's forces.

The Empire traced its origins to a [[Grand Plan|Sith conspiracy]] to destroy the [[Jedi Order]] and [[Jedi-Sith War|regain]] control over the galaxy. The Empire was secretly controlled by the [[Sith]], for the [[Galactic Emperor]] was, in fact, the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]], whose reign was enforced by his [[Sith apprentice|apprentice]], [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], whom he eventually elevated to the position of [[supreme commander of the Imperial fleet]]. Rising to power on a groundswell of populist support and capitalizing on [[Anti-Jedi sentiment|anti-Jedi]] and [[anti-droid sentiment]] and [[human]]-[[Xenophobia|ethnocentrism]] manufactured by the destructive Clone Wars, [[Darth]] Sidious appointed himself [[Emperor]] at the end of the conflict by promising security and stability to the war-torn Republic. Gaining the overwhelming approval of the [[Galactic Senate]], Darth Sidious staged a coup by the [[Jedi]] and oversaw their subsequent [[Great Jedi Purge|purge]] from the galaxy, assisted by his [[Emperor's Fist|right-hand]], Darth Vader.

The Empire stood virtually unchallenged during its rise to power, with the backing of the [[Imperial Senate]] and the spreading of its massive technological military force across the galaxy and began a major expansion and encroaching into the unexplored regions. At first, the Galactic Empire was a constitutional monarchy in basic theory, however it [[Public Order Resentencing Directive|gradually]] [[Imperial Emergency Act|evolved]] into a [[stratocracy]] as the power of the Imperial Senate waned. However, [[Rebel cell/Canon|numerous insurgent cells]] sprang up against the Empire and gradually united to initiate a [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|growing rebellion]], winning its [[Action at Mustafar|first major victory]] over [[Mustafar]] in [[4 BBY]]. These rebel groups eventually [[Declaration of Rebellion|formed]] the Rebel Alliance in [[2 BBY]], and achieved its first major victory with the [[Battle of Scarif|theft]] of the [[Death Star plans]] on [[Scarif]], which, in turn, led to the destruction of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] at the [[Battle of Yavin]]. The following years saw initial Alliance successes until a [[Battle of Hoth|major Imperial victory]] on [[Hoth]] in [[3 ABY]], but the Empire suffered a devastating defeat [[4 ABY|one year later]] at the [[Battle of Endor]]. During the battle, Darth Sidious was slain at the hands of his former disciple, the redeemed Anakin Skywalker, who himself died shortly thereafter, marking the end of Sith rule and the deterioration of the Empire and the [[Declaration of a New Republic|resumption]] of the Galactic Republic, the [[New Republic]].

With the deaths of the Emperor and his top lieutenant, factionalism overcame the Empire as it fractured into breakaway fiefdoms led by splinter [[Moff]]s, [[admiral]]s, and [[general]]s, many of whom ignored [[Grand Vizier]] [[Mas Amedda]]'s authority at the [[capital]] and became [[warlord]]s as the Empire continued to fight the Republic. The [[Imperial Navy]] came to be publicly led by loyalist [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]], though she was a figurehead for [[Fleet Admiral]] [[Gallius Rax]]. Ultimately, Rax seized control over the loyalist forces, removing Sloane from power and becoming Emperor-in-effect through his new position as [[Counselor to the Empire]]. Under Rax's command, the Empire made its final stand at the [[Battle of Jakku]] in [[5 ABY]], ultimately losing and [[Galactic Concordance|capitulating]] to the New Republic. With the cessation of the fighting, the [[Galactic Concordance]] was signed, vanquishing the Empire.

While the Empire was gone, the New Republic faced continued resistance from several Imperial remants [[9 ABY|in the years]] after. Eventually its successor, the [[First Order]] [[Project Resurrection|began]] a clandestine armament program to [[First Order military|rebuild]] the former Imperial Military. The [[First Order High Command|miltary junta]] was unaware, however, that they had been manipulated by a new hidden [[Contingency|conspiracy]], for [[Sith Eternal|secret]] [[Sith cultist|cultists]] on the lost [[Planet|world]] of [[Exegol]] attended to the [[Transference|spirit]] of Darth Sidious, and constructed a [[Final Order|fleet]] built to turn the First Order into a true [[Sith Empire|empire]]. The [[Sith cult|cult]] efforts [[Battle of Exegol|ultimately failed]], however, for they were [[First Order-Resistance War|opposed]] by the [[Resistance]] and Jedi Order, leading to an [[Uprising against the First Order|end of the First Order]].

